<ContentPage title="Now" intro="What I’m up to at the moment.">
	<p class="updated" slot="head">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11">November 2026</time></p>

	<div class="entry-list">
		<Entry title="Building this website" links={[{ label: 'Source on GitHub', href: repos.portfolio }]}>
			<p>
				You’re looking at it. It’s built with Astro, GSAP and Three.js, which is a lot of animation power for a site that
				mostly says “hire me.” It’s never quite finished, but it’s always shipping.
			</p>
			<!-- A nudge toward the sky view easter egg on the home page, without naming it (same as on Projects). -->
			<p class="entry-note">
				Psst: open the eye on <a href="/">the home page</a>, give the planet a spin, and look for the one gold thing that
				isn’t a page.
			</p>
		</Entry>
		<Entry title="A national credentialing platform">
			<p>
				I’m the full-stack engineer on a platform that verifies the credentials of fitness professionals. It handles
				payments, digital wallet passes, automated reminders and a test suite that runs on every pull request. I’d tell you
				more, but there’s an NDA, and I’d like to stay employed.
			</p>
		</Entry>
		<Entry title="A medical clinic website">
			<p>
				I’m redesigning the website for a multi-location wellness clinic and moving it off a no-code builder. That means 15
				pages, 145 services and a lot of SEO. I can’t name the client, but I can tell you their website will be much faster
				soon.
			</p>
		</Entry>
	</div>
</ContentPage>
